   $q$Which of these lines has the steepest graph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y = \\frac{1}{2}x - 9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"judged-steepness-by-largest-number"},{"text":"$y = 4x$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-negative-slopes-for-steepness"},{"text":"$y = 3x + 8$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"judged-steepness-by-intercept"},{"text":"$y = -5x + 1$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y = -5x + 1$$q$, $q$Steepness depends on the size of the slope, ignoring its sign. The slopes have sizes $5$, $4$, $3$ and $\frac{1}{2}$, so $y = -5x + 1$ is steepest; it just falls instead of rising. The line $y = 4x$ has the greatest slope as a signed number, but $4$ is smaller in size than $5$.$q$, 'draft', null)
