   $q$A club sells raffle tickets for 2 dollars each and has at most 50 tickets. The money raised is $E = 2n$, where $n$ is the number of tickets sold. Which best describes the graph for this situation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A solid segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(50, 100)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-discrete-count-as-continuous"},{"text":"Separate points from $(0, 0)$ to $(50, 100)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"A line through $(0, 0)$ and $(50, 100)$ that keeps going in both directions","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-context-domain"},{"text":"Separate points from $(0, 0)$ to $(100, 50)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-coordinates"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Separate points from $(0, 0)$ to $(50, 100)$$q$, $q$The club can only sell whole tickets from $0$ to $50$, so $n$ takes the values $0, 1, 2, \ldots, 50$. Each gives one point, ending at $(50, 2 \cdot 50) = (50, 100)$. A solid segment would include values like $n = 2.5$, which cannot happen.$q$, 'draft', null)
