   $q$A paper circle of radius $6$ cm is cut into $32$ equal sectors, which are rearranged, alternating point up and point down, into a shape close to a parallelogram. About how long is the base of that parallelogram, in centimeters?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$6$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-radius-as-base"},{"text":"$36\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-area-instead-of-base"},{"text":"$12\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-full-circumference"},{"text":"$6\\pi$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$6\pi$$q$, $q$The circumference is $2\pi \cdot 6 = 12\pi$, and half of the arcs lie along the base, so the base is about $\frac{12\pi}{2} = 6\pi$ cm. With height $6$, the area is about $6\pi \cdot 6 = 36\pi$, which is the area, not the base length.$q$, 'draft', null)
