   $q$Regular polygons with more and more sides are drawn inside a circle of radius $5$, with every vertex on the circle. As the number of sides grows, what number does the polygon's perimeter get closer and closer to?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$25\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-perimeter-with-area"},{"text":"$5\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-radius-not-diameter"},{"text":"$10\\pi$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$40$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-circumscribed-square-perimeter"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$10\pi$$q$, $q$As the sides get shorter, the polygon hugs the circle more tightly, so its perimeter approaches the circumference, $2\pi \cdot 5 = 10\pi$. The value $40$ is the perimeter of the square drawn around the circle, which is larger than the circumference and is not the limit.$q$, 'draft', null)
