   $q$A cone is cut by a plane parallel to its base, exactly halfway up its height. What fraction of the original cone's volume is in the small cone on top?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{8}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-one-third-cone-factor"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"squared-instead-of-cubed"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"scaled-linearly"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{1}{8}$$q$, $q$The small cone is similar to the original with scale factor $\frac{1}{2}$, so its radius and height are both halved. Its volume is $\frac{1}{3}\pi \left(\frac{r}{2}\right)^2 \frac{h}{2} = \frac{1}{8} \cdot \frac{1}{3}\pi r^2 h$. The fraction $\frac{1}{4}$ halves only the radius and forgets that the height is halved too.$q$, 'draft', null)
