   $q$Which expression gives the exact solution of $4 \cdot 10^x + 3 = 83$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = \\log 21.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-subtracted"},{"text":"$x = \\dfrac{\\log 80}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-the-log-by-the-coefficient"},{"text":"$x = \\log 17.75$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-before-subtracting"},{"text":"$x = \\log 20$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = \log 20$$q$, $q$Undo the steps in reverse order. Subtract $3$: $4 \cdot 10^x = 80$. Divide by $4$: $10^x = 20$. Take the common log: $x = \log 20 \approx 1.30$. The answer $\log 17.75$ divides $83$ by $4$ before subtracting the $3$, so the $3$ is never divided.$q$, 'draft', null)
