   $q$Use a calculator to solve $e^x = 0.5$. What is $x$, rounded to the nearest hundredth?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$1.65$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"applied-exponential-instead-of-log"},{"text":"$-0.30$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-common-log-for-base-e"},{"text":"$0.69$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-negative-sign"},{"text":"$-0.69$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-0.69$$q$, $q$Take the natural log: $x = \ln 0.5 \approx -0.693$, which rounds to $-0.69$. The value is negative because $e^x$ is less than $1$ only when $x < 0$. The answer $-0.30$ is $\log 0.5$, which uses base $10$ instead of base $e$.$q$, 'draft', null)
