   $q$A lab sample holds 80 grams of a substance whose amount after $t$ days is $A = 80(0.5)^{t/5}$. To the nearest hundredth of a day, when are 30 grams left?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$1.42$ days","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-multiply-by-5"},{"text":"$6.25$ days","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-linear-decay"},{"text":"$7.08$ days","is_correct":true},{"text":"$0.28$ days","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-5-instead-of-multiplying"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$7.08$ days$q$, $q$Set $80(0.5)^{t/5} = 30$ and divide by $80$: $(0.5)^{t/5} = 0.375$. Then $\dfrac{t}{5} = \dfrac{\log 0.375}{\log 0.5} \approx 1.415$, so $t \approx 5 \times 1.415 \approx 7.08$ days. The answer $6.25$ days assumes the sample loses the same 8 grams every day, but it loses half every 5 days, which is not a steady amount.$q$, 'draft', null)
